case2=pagehead(root,'Community case study','A community is built <span class="serif highlight">one person at a time.</span>','Creating supportive spaces for learners, maintaining engagement and making questions easy to ask.',True)+f'''<section class="section container case-layout"><article class="case-main"><h2>The context</h2><p>Newcomers to online business and digital learning often need a welcoming place to ask questions and understand their next step. I organized and supported Telegram and WhatsApp groups aimed at sharing practical information and peer guidance.</p><h2>The approach</h2><p>My day-to-day involvement included community announcements, onboarding-style explanations, keeping members informed, responding to common questions and helping maintain consistent participation.</p><p>I have built and supported active Telegram communities, including a 1,261-member survey group, a 2,175-member learning group and a 2,251-subscriber education channel.</p><div class="insight"><strong>Community milestones:</strong> 1,261 group members · 2,175 learning group members · 2,251 channel subscribers.</div><figure class="case-figure"><img loading="lazy" src="{root}assets/media/community-survey.webp" alt="Telegram community screenshot displaying 1,261 members"><figcaption>A community I helped build and support.</figcaption></figure><h2>What transfers into a professional team</h2><p>I bring practical experience in member onboarding, content coordination, moderation and clear, reliable support — skills I am ready to apply in larger teams.</p></article><aside class="case-aside"><dl><dt>Area</dt><dd>Community growth & engagement</dd><dt>Channels</dt><dd>Telegram, WhatsApp</dd><dt>Period</dt><dd>2025–2026</dd><dt>Community size</dt><dd>1,261 members / 2,251 subscribers</dd><dt>Work included</dt><dd>Member communication, engagement and educational guidance</dd><dt>Strength</dt><dd>Member engagement and helpful onboarding</dd></dl></aside></section>'''
